Subject: [PATCH] render_pipeline: Keep thread buffers all or nothing

LowMemoryRenderPipeline::PrepareForThreadsInternal() appended the input
buffers of a thread to group_data_ first and then allocated its channels.
When an allocation failed (memory cap), the next call started at
group_data_.size() and never allocated the missing channels, so the decoder
later wrote group data into empty planes (a JXL_DASSERT in debug builds, an
out-of-bounds write otherwise, e.g. in the noise stage's RandomImage).
Allocate all channels of a thread before adding them.

Found with djxl_fuzzer (allocation failure during a flush).
Test: RenderPipelineTest.PrepareForThreadsAfterFailedAllocation.

diff --git a/lib/jxl/render_pipeline/low_memory_render_pipeline.cc b/lib/jxl/render_pipeline/low_memory_render_pipeline.cc
index 3cd1f170..20f4eb87 100644
--- a/lib/jxl/render_pipeline/low_memory_render_pipeline.cc
+++ b/lib/jxl/render_pipeline/low_memory_render_pipeline.cc
@@ -461,16 +461,19 @@ Status LowMemoryRenderPipeline::PrepareForThreadsInternal(size_t num,
   use_group_ids_ = use_group_ids;
   size_t num_buffers = use_group_ids_ ? frame_dimensions_.num_groups : num;
   for (size_t t = group_data_.size(); t < num_buffers; t++) {
-    group_data_.emplace_back();
-    group_data_[t].resize(shifts.size());
+    // Only add the buffers of a thread (or group) once all its channels are
+    // allocated: after a failed allocation, the next call starts at
+    // group_data_.size() and would never allocate the missing channels.
+    std::vector<ImageF> data(shifts.size());
     for (size_t c = 0; c < shifts.size(); c++) {
       JXL_ASSIGN_OR_RETURN(
-          group_data_[t][c],
+          data[c],
           ImageF::Create(memory_manager_,
                          GroupInputXSize(c) + group_data_x_border_ * 2,
                          GroupInputYSize(c) + group_data_y_border_ * 2,
                          kRenderPipelineXOffset));
     }
+    group_data_.emplace_back(std::move(data));
   }
   // TODO(veluca): avoid reallocating buffers if not needed.
   stage_data_.resize(num);
